From 756a2671f7c82e6b089af251b93a5f98bce3e067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:01:09 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 40/41] VideoOutput: the stereo layer draws the drawn views
 itself into a window surface of the GPU, with no read back and no copy

The compositor's stereo layer (the declared full side by side Stereo KWin takes) had its frames converted and copied into wl_shm buffers by the
presenter's thread. For the drawn views of a depth video (frames of textures) the layer now makes an EGL context that shares the drawing context's textures,
a window surface for its wl_surface (wl_egl_window: the driver exchanges the buffers with the compositor, as DMA-BUF where both take them, with their
modifiers, release and synchronisation) and draws the two eyes with one pass: the crop, the eye order and the format of the surface, at the depth of the
views (RGBA8; RGBA16 for 10 to 16 bit content into a 10 bit or half float surface; never a surface of less depth: where the driver has none the presenter
copies through wl_shm, counted, with the reason). The drawn views carry their RGB texture (Target) for this; frames, window surface and the layer's context
live as long as the layer. QT_MM_STEREO_LAYER_SHM=1 forces the wl_shm path (the control), QT_MM_STEREO_LAYER_DUMP=dir dumps the first frames of either path
for the proofs. stereoDepthRoute says which path and why, stereoDepthReadBacks() counts the frames of each.

The matrix of a frame that does not say is the one Qt's own conversion assumes (HD BT.709, SD BT.601), and the output says it: a deep depth video of an untagged
HD stream was drawn and encoded with BT.601 and decoded by the scene graph and the presenter with BT.709 (10 bit views 2.4 % off, now 1.2 % from chroma
subsampling alone).

Tests: depthOnTheGpuKeepsTheDepth and the deep cases at 12 bits (P016, YUV422P16, YUV444P16 with the code in the high 12 bits; red when the encode pass is cut to 10 bits).

